## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 209 chars (just over cap 200) — includes parenthetical
  about non-pipeline read-only investigators. Trim.
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `intent` is 152 words (cap 100). Drop per-agent model-routing detail
  and the fixed-`brain`-key restatement.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 9 items (cap 4). Most encode contract details:
  registry-driven enumeration, exact frontmatter field list, `mcpServers:
  [brain]` declaration syntax, model-per-task-shape rule, methodology-docs-name-the-roster
  rule, command-references-agents-by-name rule. Plan/code-level.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 8 paragraph-length items, mostly enumerating
  retired regressions. Compress to 3-4.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 5 decisions (at cap) but each runs 150+ words.
  Trim to ≤80 words each.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract per-decision caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Good examples` reproduces multi-line install summary verbatim with
  exact agent names; `## Bad examples` reproduces inline MCP-config
  anti-patterns. Forbidden content.
  Traces to: examples sections | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with parent install service: registry-iteration,
  skip-existing-files, per-file status reporting, initContent chokepoint —
  parent-level invariants.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy | Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): 4 unchecked items. Re-walk after rewrite.

## Retro

installAgents bloated because the strategist treated the fixed-`brain`-MCP-key
contract as a per-agent invariant. The contract is project-wide; it lives
at the parent (or in a brain-layer parent), not in every leaf that touches
agents.
